  "id": 371787404,
  "iid": 19383,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "F1AP, Fix UL RRC Message Classification in InitialULRRCMessageTransfer",
  "description": "**Description:**  \nThis merge request fixes the classification of RRC messages inside `InitialULRRCMessageTransfer` based on the `RRCContainer` length.  \n\n**Issue:**  \nCurrently, Wireshark does not correctly differentiate between `UL-CCCH-Message` and `UL-CCCH1-Message` based on the `RRCContainer` length. According to the RRC specification:  \n- If `RRCContainer` length is **8 bytes (64 bits)** → Message is `UL-CCCH1-Message`.  \n- If `RRCContainer` length is **6 bytes (48 bits)** → Message is `UL-CCCH-Message`.  \n\n**Fix:**  \n- Updated the dissector logic to check the `RRCContainer` length inside `InitialULRRCMessageTransfer`.  \n- If the length is **8 bytes**, classify it as `UL-CCCH1-Message`.  \n- If the length is **6 bytes**, classify it as `UL-CCCH-Message`.  \n- Ensure proper labeling in the Wireshark UI.  \n\n**Testing:**  \n- Verified with sample PCAP files containing `InitialULRRCMessageTransfer` messages.  \n- Ensured correct message classification in the decoded output.  \n- PCAP Link https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zKa-yV3cXcM0EfbLQbrKJq7T7KPai1LN/view?usp=sharing\n\n**Screenshots:**\n- With Fix\n- ![image](/uploads/6a2d38a728c03892ccf28cc20e30a633/image.png)\n\n**Impact:**  \n- Fixes incorrect RRC message decoding.  \n- Improves accuracy of 5G RRC message analysis.  \n\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to draft the actual code changes for Wireshark’s dissector as well?",
